-- title:
--   Igusa-side prolongation traces to the Gauss reduction at level M'
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$. $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ in $A$ is a non-unit, so that $A$ has residue characteristic $q$; its residue field is written $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur: the level-$M'$ field $\overline{F}_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $q$-expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$), and the full-level field $\overline{F} =$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the corresponding base change of the function field of the $X_H$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\overline{F}_{M'} \le \overline{F}$, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` is the resulting embedding. The element $\hat\jmath \in \overline{F}_{M'}$ is the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Finally $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa_A$ which by `hW` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, of those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have `w.evalAt (jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M')` in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; and $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, the agreement `algebraMap_mem_iff` of `R₀.integers` with $A$ on constants and the compatibility `residue_algebraMap` of residues on constants, the scaling axiom `exists_smul_mem`, and the divisor-pushforward axiom `mapDomain_placeMap`. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with the Gauss (coefficientwise) reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image `coeffMap A.subtype y` lies in $\overline{F}_{M'}$, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue ↥A) y`.
--
--   The Gauss-uniqueness hypothesis `hGU` states that `R₀.integers` is the only valuation subring $V$ of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ with the following three properties: $V$ agrees with $A$ on constants (for $a \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $a$ lies in $V$ iff $a \in A$); $\hat\jmath \in V$; and $\hat\jmath$ is residually transcendental in the sense that for every polynomial $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(\hat\jmath)$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$, then every coefficient of $p$ has its image in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$. Under these three conditions $V$ and `R₀.integers` have the same elements.
--
--   The base-field data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`). Writing $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation ring of $k_0$, it is assumed that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is Henselian local (`hhens`), that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   $\overline{F}$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline{F}$. The assertion is then made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{F}$ satisfying two conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants (the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline{F}$) is all of $\overline{F}$; and a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{F}$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ then every $a_i$ vanishes.
--
--   Next, $W_0$ is a valuation subring of $F_0$ subject to the conjunction of: agreement with $A$ on $k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ iff the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$); $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Further, $O$ is a subring of $F_0$ which is local and Noetherian, such that $O \subseteq W_0$, such that $O$ agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ in the same sense, such that every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant modulo the maximal ideal — for each $f \in O$ there is $x \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose image lies in $O$ with $f - x$ not a unit of $O$ — and such that $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$: every $f \in F_0$ can be written with $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \ne 0$.
--
--   The crossing data are: a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$; the image $\pi_O \in O$ of $\pi_0$; elements $c_x, c_y \in O$; a unit $u$ of $O$; a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ with parameter the $E_0$-th power of the image of $\pi_0$, i.e. onto $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$; and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that quotient. They are required to satisfy: $c_x c_y = \pi_O^{E_0} u$; compatibility of $\iota$ with constants, namely for $x \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with image in $O$, $\iota$ sends the image of $x$ in the completion to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\widehat{A_0}$; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$ for the classes $U, V$ of the two variables; $c_y \in W_0$, with $c_y$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, and $c_x$ not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ whenever it lies in $W_0$.
--
--   The Igusa branch is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ subject to: $O \subseteq W_x$; agreement with $A$ on $k_0$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; the existence of a residually transcendental parameter, namely some $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then the image of every coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal; $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ whenever it lies in $W_x$, and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$ whenever it lies in $W_x$; and finally the law relating $W_x$ to the level-$M'$ reduction: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image $\hat g \in \overline{F}_{M'}$ lies in `R₀.integers` and which satisfies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\hat g)$ at every place $P$ of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\hat\jmath)$, the image of $\hat g$ in $\overline{F}$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if `R₀.residue` $\hat g = 0$, and, should `R₀.residue` $\hat g$ lie in the valuation subring of the place $s$, that element lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with image in $O$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals `s.evalAt (R₀.residue ĝ)`, the difference of the element and $c$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   Under all of the above, for every field $FI$ with a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure and every `RegularProlongation A ↥(fieldBar q M') FI` $R_x$ — a valuation subring `Rx.integers` of $\overline{F}$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $FI$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, agreeing with $A$ on constants, compatible with residues of constants, and satisfying the scaling axiom — whose trace on $F_0$ is $W_x$, in the sense that for all $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `Rx.integers` iff $f \in W_x$, the conclusion is the single biconditional: for every $f \in \overline{F}_{M'}$, the image of $f$ in $\overline{F}$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in `Rx.integers` if and only if $f$ lies in `R₀.integers`. Thus the trace of $R_x$ on the level-$M'$ field is exactly the Gauss reduction ring $R_0$.
--
--   This is the sharp form of the integrality statement for an Igusa-side end of the semistable reduction at level $q^2M'$: it identifies the trace on the level-$M'$ modular function field of any regular prolongation of $A$ whose trace on $F_0$ is the Igusa branch $W_x$ with the Gauss (coefficientwise) reduction $R_0$, both inclusions being asserted. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch), where only one of the two implications appears among that statement's conjuncts; the proof invokes the transcendence of `jqModC`, the algebraicity of residue fields of valuation subrings of algebraic extensions of $\mathbb Q$ over $\mathbb F_q$, and the algebraic closedness of the residue field of a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
